{"title":"Strict inequality","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Strict_inequality&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p><p>A strict <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Inequality\" title=\"Inequality\">inequality</a> is an inequality where the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Inequality_symbol\" title=\"Inequality symbol\">inequality symbol</a> is either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/f/77f0cdbd0dbecd281387229d95a014017a0a395a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&gt;$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> (greater than) or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/2/262a080d0d87e973b817945967a512346d8bfc49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt;$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> (less than).  That is, a strict inequality is an inequality which has no <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Equality_condition\" title=\"Equality condition\">equality conditions</a>.  \n</p><p>For example: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/d/66db4e19b3be56d841f02880243f258ec5d1e88b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> <i>is</i> a strict inequality. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e3e39b6baea8e7b5a17b25bc3a9a55f2fa0a4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\geq1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" /> is <i>not</i> a strict inequality.\n</p><p>An example of a well-known strict inequality is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle_Inequality\" title=\"Triangle Inequality\">Triangle Inequality</a>, which states that, in a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nondegenerate\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Nondegenerate\">nondegenerate</a> triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, the following relation holds:\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/8/c5869fd58dc25499fdad1662705c4d4321d43ff2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB+BC&gt;AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"131\" height=\"14\" /></center>\n<p>A non-example is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Trivial_Inequality\" title=\"Trivial Inequality\">Trivial Inequality</a> which states that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real_number\" title=\"Real number\">real number</a> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/1/16140d5c166c1466d0fe5fad7d950adfa2aa7c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"17\" />.  This inequality is not strict because it has an equality case: when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d348bde3e15456e71734dc2c56fc7425c95927f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/c/37c225805139ae949ab88655549cf677d2b264e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 = 0$\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018111235\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.016 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 37/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 292/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1727/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.118      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    6.118      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3536:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018111235 and revision id 132991. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}